<title>ABU DHABI: Mitsui, BP, Total ADGAS stakes cut.</title>
<headline>Mitsui, BP, Total ADGAS stakes cut.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui, British Petroleum and Total stakes in Abu Dhabi Gas Liquefaction Co (ADGAS) have been cut in a redistribution of equity, officials said.</p>
<p>Abu Dhabi National Oil Co (ADNOC) said in a statement the country's Supreme Petroleum Council had decided to increase ADNOC's share in ADGAS to 70 percent from 51 percent.</p>
<p>Mitsui will now have around 15 percent from a previous 24.5 percent, BP will have 10 percent from 16.33 and Total will have a five percent stake from 8.17 previously, an industry official said.</p>
<p>ADGAS, which runs a liquefaction plant at Das Island and was set up in 1973, has annual revenues of around $1.65 billion, the official said. He said the changes in the equity structure had been under discussion for the past four years.</p>
</text>
